 frame="The Nebraska Department of Environment and Energy administers the program and certifies professionals.",
 geology="Loess soils across the east with moderate to slow percolation, sandhills in the centre and northwest with very fast-draining sand, and clay in the southeast. Groundwater depth varies enormously.",
 systems="Conventional trenches and lagoons, with lagoons still common on rural acreages. In the sandhills, excessive permeability requires attention to treatment rather than disposal capacity.",
 permit="Nebraska certifies environmental professionals to conduct site evaluations and design systems, and requires registration of systems. Setbacks from wells are strictly enforced given the reliance on groundwater.",
