 systems="Conventional trenches and seepage pits, the latter still permitted in circumstances many states have abandoned. Advanced treatment where nitrogen loading to a shallow aquifer is a concern.",
 permit="The two urban health authorities — Southern Nevada Health District covering Clark County and Washoe County Health District — have their own requirements, and they cover most of the state's population. Rural counties fall under NDEP.",
 counties=[("Clark","Las Vegas; Southern Nevada Health District administers"),
           ("Washoe","Reno; county health district with its own program"),
           ("Douglas","Carson valley, nitrate concerns"),
           ("Lyon","Rural growth on alluvial soils"),
           ("Nye","Pahrump valley; large septic population over an aquifer")],
 pump="Advanced systems require maintenance under district requirements.",
